
## Operator workflow

1. Run `bin/simple test test/01_unit/compiler/common/di_spec.spl`.
2. Every scenario must pass; a failure is a regression in the
   behavior under test.

## Compatibility and limitations

Covers the interpreter and native lanes for the constructs
asserted here; platform-specific behavior is out of scope.
"""

        it("locks reject further bindings", fn() -> ():
            # @req REQ-SSPEC-UNIT
            step("lock the container and attempt a bind")
            val di = DiContainer.for_profile(CompilerProfile.Test)
            di.lock()
            di.bind("X", \: 1)
            expect(di.is_locked()).to_equal(true)
            expect(di.has_binding("X")).to_equal(false)
        )
    )
